essentialSupport.fact:
Alongside Main.java create study/Labels.java with the code below. Compile with javac --release 25 -d classes Main.java study/Labels.java, then run java -cp classes Main. The class path points to the root above study, not to the study folder.
```java
package study;
public class Labels {
  public static String name() { return "review"; }
}
```

Compile javac --release 25 -d classes Main.java tools/Scale.java; run java -cp classes Main. A real third-party build should record dependency versions and repositories, not rely on an accidental IDE class path. Here the exact helper is:
```java
package tools;
public class Scale {
  public static int doubleIt(int value) { return value * 2; }
}
```
